      "en": "Little or Temminck's Stint?"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Temminck's is plain and cold brown-grey above and across the breast, with yellow-green legs and no pale V on the back. Little Stint has black legs and (in juvenile) a rusty back with a clean white V. In flight Temminck's shows white outer tail feathers, and its call is a dry trill, not a sharp 'tit'."
